{{Yang is a cheerful, energetic, and bright young lady. She is arguably the most flippant, carefree, and adventurous member of her team, frequently making sarcastic comments and jokes even in the heat of battle and often taking combat and hostile situations lightly. Yang is very sociable and extroverted, even in unfamiliar situations. Yang's love of adventure is the main reason that she decided to become a Huntress. Blake considers Yang the personification of the word "strength". Yang also has a hot temper.}}

{{She also has a good degree of heroism and selflessness.}}

{{Yang likes to make puns to lighten the mood.}}

{{Yang has a love for puns and sometimes playfully flirts with her friends, but she never takes it too far and stops when people ask her to stop.}}

{{She is very straightforward and confident.}}

{{Yang is very sociable and extroverted, even in unfamiliar situations.}}

{{Yang can be extremely flirtatious.}}

{{Yang's love of adventure is the main reason that she decided to become a Huntress.}}

{{Yang is also very protective of her hair, becoming enraged when someone touches or rips or cuts even a small portion of her hair, causing her to attack with straight, blunt force the one who did it.}}

{{Yang's mother, Raven Branwen, left Yang and her father when she was a child.}}

{{Yang's step-mother, Summer Rose, left for a mission and never returned, presumably dead. Ruby visits her grave often.}}

{{Yang's father is Taiyang Xiao Long, usually just going by Tai, is a stay at home father.}}

{{Yang is extremely sensitive about being abandoned and her "simmering anger" stems from these abandonment issues. For the better part of nearly two decades, Yang spent her life searching for her mother, trying to understand her reasons for leaving. Yang no longer cares why her mother left and has moved passed it.}}

{{Yang is quite mature. She is extremely nurturing and motherly, particularly toward her younger sister, Ruby.}}

{{According to Taiyang, Yang shares a flaw with her mother: thinking strength is all that matters in a fight.}}

{{Despite her tendency to run into fights and danger on a whim, Yang is far from stupid, she is pretty smart in her own right.}}

{{Yang's semblance, named Burn, allows her to absorb hits from her opponent and power herself up and send it back with even greater force. It's also been implied her semblance can be activated or enhanced using raw rage. Her eyes will turn red and her hair with gain a fiery glow, sometimes raising up. At it's absolute strongest it's been shown to destroy mechs.}}

{{While taking hits from an opponent vastly increases the power of her Semblance, Yang still takes damage in the process. Despite her high reserves of Aura, too many hits can deplete it completely, breaking her defenses and rendering her Semblance counterattack useless. Conversely, activating her Semblance too soon will also weaken her Aura's defenses in exchange for an under-charged counterstrike. Yang is also noted to be weak against kick-based fighting styles.}}

{{Fighters well-versed in dodging attacks can frustrate Yang, making her attacks predictable and easily avoided, which also renders the added power with her Semblance useless. The fact that she fights barehanded as opposed to using a melee weapon also limits the reach of her close-quarters attacks, enabling opponents with greater agility to evade her strikes.}}

{{Yang is a tall, busty, thin and muscular young woman. She has large breasts. She is 5'8" tall. She has long and wavy blonde hair with a cowlick on the top of her head. She has fair skin. She has lilac eyes. When her semblance is active, her eyes turn red and her hair gains a fiery glow, and sometimes raises into the air. She greatly resembles her birth mother Raven Branwen.}}

{{Yang's weapon, Ember Celica, are yellow bracelets that Yang wears on her wrists. The bracelets and transform and turn into gauntlets. Ember Celica uses shotgun shells to give Yang's punches extra power. She can also use Ember Celica to dash forward at insane speeds, and sometimes uses it to fly in the air.}}
